#: lib/utility.php:1150
msgid "MySQL 5.6+ and MariaDB 10.0+ are great releases, and are very good versions to choose. Make sure you run the very latest release though which fixes a long standing low level networking issue that was causing spine many issues with reliability."
msgstr "MySQL 5.6+ na MariaDB 10.0+ ni verisiyo nziza cyane zo guhitamo. Nyamuneka menya neza ko ukoresha verisiyo ya vuba cyane ikemura ikibazo cyo mu rwego rwo hasi cy'urusobe cyamaze igihe kirekire cyateraga Spine ibibazo byinshi byo kutizerwa."

#: lib/utility.php:1162
#, php-format
msgid "It is STRONGLY recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.5.3."
msgstr "Birashishikarizwa CYANE gushoboza InnoDB muri verisiyo iyo ari yo yose ya %s irenze 5.5.3."

#: lib/utility.php:1175 lib/utility.php:1212
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4_unicode_ci collation type as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Iyo ukoresha Cacti mu zindi ndimi zitari Icyongereza, ni ngombwa gukoresha ubwoko bw'ishyirahamwe rya utf8mb4_unicode_ci kuko inyuguti zimwe zitwara hejuru ya bayiti imwe."

#: lib/utility.php:1181 lib/utility.php:1187 lib/utility.php:1218
#: lib/utility.php:1224
msgid "When using Cacti with languages other than English, it is important to use the utf8mb4 character set as some characters take more than a single byte."
msgstr "Iyo ukoresha Cacti mu zindi ndimi zitari Icyongereza, ni ngombwa gukoresha itsinda ry'inyuguti rya utf8mb4 kuko inyuguti zimwe zitwara hejuru ya bayiti imwe."

#: lib/utility.php:1200
#, php-format
msgid "It is recommended that you enable InnoDB in any %s version greater than 5.1."
msgstr "Birashishikarizwa gushoboza InnoDB muri verisiyo iyo ari yo yose ya %s irenze 5.1."

#: lib/utility.php:1233
#, php-format
msgid "Depending on the number of logins and use of spine data collector, %s will need many connections.  The calculation for spine is: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), then you must leave headroom for user connections, which will change depending on the number of concurrent login accounts."
msgstr "Ugendeye ku mubare w'abinjira n'ikoreshwa ry'ikusanyamakuru rya Spine, %s izakenera ukwihuza kwinshi. Imibare ya Spine ni: total_connections = total_processes * (total_threads + script_servers + 1), hanyuma ugomba gusiga umwanya w'inyongera w'ukwihuza kw'abakoresha, bihindagurika bitewe n'umubare w'amakonti yinjira icyarimwe."

#: lib/utility.php:1238
msgid "Keeping the table cache larger means less file open/close operations when using innodb_file_per_table."
msgstr "Kugira ububiko bw'imbonerahamwe bunini bisobanura ibikorwa bike byo gufungura/gufunga dosiye igihe ukoresha innodb_file_per_table."

#: lib/utility.php:1243
msgid "With Remote polling capabilities, large amounts of data will be synced from the main server to the remote pollers.  Therefore, keep this value at or above 16M."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ubushobozi bwo gukusanya amakuru ku mbuga za kure, amakuru menshi azahuzwa kuva kuri seriveri nkuru ajya ku bikusanya amakuru bya kure. Kubera iyo mpamvu, gumisha aka gaciro kuri 16M cyangwa hejuru yayo."

#: lib/utility.php:1249
#, php-format
msgid "If using the Cacti Performance Booster and choosing a memory storage engine, you have to be careful to flush your Performance Booster buffer before the system runs out of memory table space.  This is done two ways, first reducing the size of your output column to just the right size.  This column is in the tables poller_output, and poller_output_boost.  The second thing you can do is allocate more memory to memory tables.  We have arbitrarily chosen a recommended value of 10%% of system memory, but if you are using SSD disk drives, or have a smaller system, you may ignore this recommendation or choose a different storage engine.  You may see the expected consumption of the Performance Booster tables under Console -> System Utilities -> View Boost Status."
msgstr "Niba ukoresha Cacti Performance Booster kandi ugahitamo moteri yo kubika mu bubiko bw'igihe gito (memory), ugomba kwitonda ukanyanyagiza ububiko bwa Performance Booster mbere y'uko sisitemu ishira umwanya w'imbonerahamwe zo mu bubiko. Ibi bikorwa mu buryo bubiri: ubwa mbere ni ukugabanya ingano y'inkingi y'ibisohoka ikagera ku ngano nyayo. Iyi nkingi iri mu mbonerahamwe poller_output, na poller_output_boost. Icya kabiri wakora ni ugushyira ububiko bwinshi ku mbonerahamwe zo mu bubiko. Twahisemo mu buryo busanzwe agaciro gashishikarizwa ka 10%% by'ububiko bwa sisitemu, ariko niba ukoresha disiki za SSD, cyangwa ufite sisitemu ntoya, ushobora kwirengagiza iyi nama cyangwa ugahitamo indi moteri yo kubika. Ushobora kureba ikoreshwa ryitezwe ry'imbonerahamwe za Performance Booster munsi ya Console -> Ibikoresho bya Sisitemu -> Reba Imimerere ya Boost."

#: lib/utility.php:1255
msgid "When executing subqueries, having a larger temporary table size, keep those temporary tables in memory."
msgstr "Iyo ukora ibibazo byungirije (subqueries), kugira ingano nini y'imbonerahamwe z'igihe gito bituma izo mbonerahamwe z'igihe gito ziguma mu bubiko (memory)."

#: lib/utility.php:1261 lib/utility.php:1267
msgid "When performing joins, if they are below this size, they will be kept in memory and never written to a temporary file.  As this is a per connection memory allocation, care must be taken not to increase it too high.  The sum of the join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + Core MySQL/MariaDB memory should be below 80%.  If the recommendation is negative, you must decrease this and or the sort_buffer_size until the recommendation fits within the allowable memory."
msgstr "Iyo ukora ihuza ry'imbonerahamwe (joins), niba biri munsi y'iyi ngano, bizaguma mu bubiko (memory) kandi ntibizigera byandikwa muri dosiye y'igihe gito. Kubera ko iri ari igenerwa ry'ububiko kuri buri kwihuza, hagomba kwitonderwa kutaryongera cyane. Igiteranyo cya join_buffer_size + sort_buffer_size + read_buffer_size + read_rnd_buffer_size + thread_stack + binlog_cache_size + ububiko bw'ibanze bwa MySQL/MariaDB kigomba kuba munsi ya 80%. Niba igitekerezo gitangwa ari munsi ya zeru, ugomba kugabanya iki na/cyangwa sort_buffer_size kugeza igihe igitekerezo gihuye n'ububiko bwemewe."

#: lib/utility.php:1273
#, php-format
msgid "When using InnoDB storage it is important to keep your table spaces separate.  This makes managing the tables simpler for long time users of %s.  If you are running with this currently off, you can migrate to the per file storage by enabling the feature, and then running an alter statement on all InnoDB tables."
msgstr "Iyo ukoresha ububiko bwa InnoDB ni ngombwa gutandukanya imyanya y'imbonerahamwe. Ibi byorohereza imicungire y'imbonerahamwe ku bakoresha ba %s igihe kirekire. Niba kuri ubu ukoresha ibi bifunze, ushobora kwimukira ku bubiko bwa buri dosiye ushobora iki gikorwa, hanyuma ugakora itegeko rya alter ku mbonerahamwe zose za InnoDB."

#: lib/utility.php:1279
msgid "When using innodb_file_per_table, it is important to set the innodb_file_format to Barracuda.  This setting will allow longer indexes important for certain Cacti tables."
msgstr "Iyo ukoresha innodb_file_per_table, ni ngombwa gushyira innodb_file_format kuri Barracuda. Iri genamiterere rizemerera indangamurongo ndende z'ingenzi ku mbonerahamwe zimwe na zimwe za Cacti."

#: lib/utility.php:1285
msgid "If your tables have very large indexes, you must operate with the Barracuda innodb_file_format and the innodb_large_prefix equal to 1.  Failure to do this may result in plugins that can not properly create tables."
msgstr "Niba imbonerahamwe zawe zifite indangamurongo nini cyane, ugomba gukoresha innodb_file_format ya Barracuda na innodb_large_prefix bingana na 1. Kutabikora bishobora gutuma imigereka idashobora gukora imbonerahamwe neza."

#: lib/utility.php:1291
#, php-format
msgid "InnoDB will hold as much tables and indexes in system memory as is possible.  Therefore, you should make the innodb_buffer_pool large enough to hold as much of the tables and index in memory.  Checking the size of the /var/lib/mysql/cacti directory will help in determining this value.  We are recommending 25%% of your systems total memory, but your requirements will vary depending on your systems size."
msgstr "InnoDB izabika imbonerahamwe n'indangamurongo nyinshi zishoboka mu bubiko bwa sisitemu. Kubera iyo mpamvu, ugomba kugira innodb_buffer_pool nini bihagije kugira ngo ibike imbonerahamwe n'indangamurongo nyinshi mu bubiko. Kureba ingano y'ububiko bwa /var/lib/mysql/cacti bizagufasha kumenya aka gaciro. Turashishikariza 25%% by'ububiko bwose bwa sisitemu yawe, ariko ibyo ukeneye bizatandukana bitewe n'ingano ya sisitemu yawe."

#: lib/utility.php:1297
msgid "This settings should remain ON unless your Cacti instances is running on either ZFS or FusionI/O which both have internal journaling to accommodate abrupt system crashes.  However, if you have very good power, and your systems rarely go down and you have backups, turning this setting to OFF can net you almost a 50% increase in database performance."
msgstr "Iri genamiterere rikwiye kuguma kuri ON keretse niba Cacti yawe ikorera kuri ZFS cyangwa FusionI/O, zombi zifite uburyo bwazo bwo gukurikirana impinduka (journaling) bufasha igihe sisitemu izimye bitunguranye.  Icyakora, niba ufite umuriro w'amashanyarazi wizewe cyane, sisitemu zawe zikaba zitajya zihagarara kandi ukaba ufite kopi z'amakuru (backups), gushyira iri genamiterere kuri OFF bishobora kongera imikorere y'ububiko bw'amakuru ku kigero cya hafi mirongo itanu ku ijana (50%)."

#: lib/utility.php:1302
msgid "This is where metadata is stored. If you had a lot of tables, it would be useful to increase this."
msgstr "Aha ni ho amakuru asobanura ayandi (metadata) abikwa. Niba ufite imbonerahamwe nyinshi, byaba byiza kongera iki."

#: lib/utility.php:1307
msgid "Rogue queries should not for the database to go offline to others.  Kill these queries before they kill your system."
msgstr "Ibibazo bibi by'ububiko bw'amakuru ntibigomba gutuma ububiko bw'amakuru buva ku murongo ku bandi. Hagarika ibi bibazo mbere y'uko bihagarika sisitemu yawe."

#: lib/utility.php:1312
msgid "Maximum I/O performance happens when you use the O_DIRECT method to flush pages."
msgstr "Imikorere myiza cyane ya I/O ibaho igihe ukoresha uburyo bwa O_DIRECT mu kohereza impapuro kuri disiki."

#: lib/utility.php:1322
#, php-format
msgid "Setting this value to 2 means that you will flush all transactions every second rather than at commit.  This allows %s to perform writing less often."
msgstr "Gushyira aka gaciro kuri 2 bisobanura ko uzajya wohereza ibikorwa byose buri segonda aho kuba igihe byemejwe (commit). Ibi bituma %s ikora igikorwa cyo kwandika gake gashoboka."

#: lib/utility.php:1327
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ububiko bugezweho bw'ubwoko bwa SSD, kugira imirongo myinshi ya I/O bitanga inyungu ku porogaramu zifite imikorere myinshi ya I/O."

#: lib/utility.php:1335 lib/utility.php:1377
#, php-format
msgid "As of %s %s, the you can control how often %s flushes transactions to disk.  The default is 1 second, but in high I/O systems setting to a value greater than 1 can allow disk I/O to be more sequential"
msgstr "Guhera kuri %s %s, ushobora kugenzura incuro %s yohereza ibikorwa kuri disiki. Ibisanzwe ni isegonda 1, ariko muri sisitemu zifite I/O nyinshi gushyira agaciro karenze 1 bishobora gutuma I/O ya disiki ikurikirana neza"

#: lib/utility.php:1340
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ububiko bugezweho bw'ubwoko bwa SSD, kugira imirongo myinshi yo gusoma ya I/O bitanga inyungu ku porogaramu zifite imikorere myinshi ya I/O. Bitewe na verisiyo zawe za MariaDB/MySQL, aka gaciro gashobora kugera kuri 64. Ariko gerageza gutuma umubare uba munsi y'umubare wose wa SMT threads kuri seriveri y'ububiko bw'amakuru."

#: lib/utility.php:1345
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics.  Depending on your MariaDB/MySQL versions, this value can go as high as 64.  But try to keep the number less than your total SMT threads on the database server."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ububiko bugezweho bw'ubwoko bwa SSD, kugira imirongo myinshi yo kwandika ya I/O bitanga inyungu ku porogaramu zifite imikorere myinshi ya I/O. Bitewe na verisiyo zawe za MariaDB/MySQL, aka gaciro gashobora kugera kuri 64. Ariko gerageza gutuma umubare uba munsi y'umubare wose wa SMT threads kuri seriveri y'ububiko bw'amakuru."

#: lib/utility.php:1351
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MariaDB less than 10.5.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s izagabanyamo innodb_buffer_pool mu bice by'ububiko kugira ngo yongere imikorere kuri verisiyo za MariaDB ziri munsi ya 10.5. Agaciro ntarengwa ni 64, ariko ntikagomba kurenga umubare wa CPU cores/threads. Iyo innodb_buffer_pool yawe iri munsi ya 1GB, ugomba gukoresha ingano y'ikigega igabanyijwe na 128MB. Komeza ukoreshe iyi mibare kugeza ku mubare ntarengwa wa CPU cores cyangwa 64."

#: lib/utility.php:1351
#, php-format
msgid "%s will divide the innodb_buffer_pool into memory regions to improve performance for versions of MySQL upto and including MySQL 8.0.  The max value is 64, but should not exceed more than the number of CPU cores/threads.  When your innodb_buffer_pool is less than 1GB, you should use the pool size divided by 128MB.  Continue to use this equation up to the max of the number of CPU cores or 64."
msgstr "%s izagabanyamo innodb_buffer_pool mu bice by'ububiko kugira ngo yongere imikorere kuri verisiyo za MySQL kugeza no kuri MySQL 8.0. Agaciro ntarengwa ni 64, ariko ntikagomba kurenga umubare wa CPU cores/threads. Iyo innodb_buffer_pool yawe iri munsi ya 1GB, ugomba gukoresha ingano y'ikigega igabanyijwe na 128MB. Komeza ukoreshe iyi mibare kugeza ku mubare ntarengwa wa CPU cores cyangwa 64."

#: lib/utility.php:1357 lib/utility.php:1393
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 200 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 100000 can be used."
msgstr "Niba ufite disiki za SSD, koresha iki gitekerezo. Niba ufite disiki zisanzwe zikarishye, koresha 200 * umubare wa disiki zikora mu murongo wazo. Niba ukoresha NVMe cyangwa PCIe Flash, imibare minini cyane ishobora kugera ku 100000 irashobora gukoreshwa."

#: lib/utility.php:1363 lib/utility.php:1399
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion.  If you have physical hard drives, use 2000 * the number of active drives in the array.  If using NVMe or PCIe Flash, much larger numbers as high as 200000 can be used."
msgstr "Niba ufite disiki za SSD, koresha iki gitekerezo. Niba ufite disiki zisanzwe zikarishye, koresha 2000 * umubare wa disiki zikora mu murongo wazo. Niba ukoresha NVMe cyangwa PCIe Flash, imibare minini cyane ishobora kugera ku 200000 irashobora gukoreshwa."

#: lib/utility.php:1369 lib/utility.php:1405
msgid "If you have SSD disks, use this suggestion. Otherwise, do not set this setting."
msgstr "Niba ufite disiki za SSD, koresha iki gitekerezo. Bitabaye ibyo, ntushyireho iri genamiterere."

#: lib/utility.php:1382
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple read io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ububiko bugezweho bw'ubwoko bwa SSD, kugira imirongo myinshi yo gusoma ya I/O bitanga inyungu ku porogaramu zifite imikorere myinshi ya I/O."

#: lib/utility.php:1387
msgid "With modern SSD type storage, having multiple write io threads is advantageous for applications with high io characteristics."
msgstr "Hamwe n'ububiko bugezweho bw'ubwoko bwa SSD, kugira imirongo myinshi yo kwandika ya I/O bitanga inyungu ku porogaramu zifite imikorere myinshi ya I/O."

#: lib/utility.php:1418
msgid "When using MariaDB 10.2.4 and above, this setting should be off if atomic writes are enabled.  Therefore, please enable atomic writes instead of the double write buffer as it will increase performance."
msgstr "Iyo ukoresha MariaDB 10.2.4 no hejuru yayo, iri genamiterere rigomba kuba rifunze niba atomic writes zishobojwe. Kubera iyo mpamvu, nyamuneka shoboza atomic writes aho gukoresha double write buffer kuko bizongera imikorere."

#: lib/utility.php:1425
